{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-05-Jul-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "12 : 15 : 20", "added": false}, {"text": "15 : 20 : 12", "added": false}, {"text": "20 : 12 : 15", "added": false}, {"text": "20 : 15 : 12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "An equal sum of money was lent to P and Q at 8.6% per annum for a period of 7 years and 8 years, respectively. If the difference in interest paid by them was ₹172, then the sum lent to each was:", "options": [{"text": "₹3,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,150", "added": false}, {"text": "₹185", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A chord of length 12 units in a circle of radius 10 units is ______ units away from its centre.", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Raju spends 80% of his income. His income increased by 20%, while his spending rise by 10%. The percentage of increase in his savings is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "The sum of two−digit number and the number obtained by interchanging the digit is 77. If the difference of digits is 1, then the number is:", "options": [{"text": "67", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "factors-divisors", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A solid copper sphere of radius 9 cm is drawn into a wire of radius 4 mm. Find the length of the wire.", "options": [{"text": "60.75 m", "added": false}, {"text": "70.25 m", "added": false}, {"text": "65.25 m", "added": false}, {"text": "20.75 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The radii of two concentric circles are 35 cm and 21 cm. If the chord of the greater circle is a tangent to the smaller circle, then the length of that chord is:", "options": [{"text": "70 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "42 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "56 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "28 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The diameter of the base of a cylindrical tank is 28 cm and its height is 42 cm. Find its curved surface area.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "paths-and-borders", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "Write the smallest digit in the blank space of a number 7__7624, so that the number formed is divisible by 3.", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "A number is first increased by 44% and then decreased by 30%. The net percentage change (rounded off to the nearest integer) in the original number is:", "options": [{"text": "increase by 1%", "added": false}, {"text": "decrease by 4%", "added": false}, {"text": "increase by 4%", "added": false}, {"text": "decrease by 1%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "98%", "added": false}, {"text": "28%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "70%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "PQ is a chord of a circle. The tangent XR at point X on the circle intersects the extension of PQ at point R. Given that XR = 12 cm, PQ = x cm, and QR = (x - 2) cm, find the value of x.", "options": [{"text": "11 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "10 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "∆ABC and ∆DEF are similar and their areas are respectively 0.64 m2 and 0.0121 m2. If EF = 0.154 m, then BC is:", "options": [{"text": "1.15 m", "added": false}, {"text": "11.2 m", "added": false}, {"text": "1.12 m", "added": false}, {"text": "2.12 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "paths-and-borders", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "In an election between two candidates, one candidate gets 72% of the total votes cast. If the total votes are 1000, by how many votes does the winner win the election?", "options": [{"text": "360", "added": false}, {"text": "250", "added": false}, {"text": "720", "added": false}, {"text": "440", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "The average age of 24 workers and their supervisor is 41 years. If the supervisor's age is excluded, the average reduces by 0.75 years. The age of the supervisor is:", "options": [{"text": "59 years", "added": false}, {"text": "41 years 9 months", "added": false}, {"text": "40 years 9 months", "added": false}, {"text": "49 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": null}]}